210102   1 NNN         00000001000psch                                    000317
25Disinfection of the overall plant                                       000318
26   Professional disinfection and subsequent flushing of                 000319
26   all plant parts in the scope of supply that are in                   000320
26   contact with drinking water, incl. pumps, surge                      000321
26   vessels, filter vessels and clean water tanks and other              000322
26   units and valves, for commissioning with proof of                    000323
26   freedom from germs by a certified laboratory.                        000324
26                                                                        000325
26   Required are at least 3 samples in succession with                   000326
26   negative biological findings (scope of examination                   000327
26   Pseudomonas aeruginosa, PER000160 bacteria, Escherichia              000328
26   coli, enterococci, culturable microorganisms as colony               000329
26   count at 22 øC and 36 øC).                                           000330
26                                                                        000331
26   The proof samples are to be taken at the raw water                   000332
26   inlet and at the clean water outlet of the waterworks                000333
26   (i.e. 3 samplings at 2 sampling points each).                        000334
26                                                                        000335
26   Execution in several stages according to the                         000336
26   requirements of the plant configuration.                             000337
26                                                                        000338
26   The billing of any further disinfections required is on              000339
26   the basis of actual time and material against proof,                 000340
26   but only as far as the contractor is not responsible                 000341
26   for the repeated disinfection.                                       000342
26                                                                        000343
26   Note on vessel disinfection (filters):                               000344
26   The disinfection of the filter bed of the arsenic                    000345
26   removal filters is dealt with in a separate item in the              000346
26   division "Equipment arsenication filters".                           000347
26   The AN alone is responsible for the harmless disposal                000348
26   of the waste water including any neutralisation                      000349
26   required.                                                            000350
26   It is to be taken into account that the property                     000351
26   drainage (wastewater) is by means of a lifting unit,                 000352
26   which is designed for a delivery rate of approx. 8                   000353
26   m3/h. The disposal of larger quantities of waste water               000354
26   is therefore possibly associated with a higher                       000355
26   expenditure of time, unless buffer tanks for the                     000356
26   intermediate storage of waste water are kept available               000357
26   on site.                                                             000358
26   For the period of the disinfection it is to be assumed               000359
26   for the cost estimate that no valves are yet                         000360
26   electrically connected, i.e. corresponding expenditure               000361
26   of time for manual on-site operation is to be included               000362
26   in the price and is not paid separately.                             000363
26                                                                        000364
26   Disinfectant e.g. [PERSON_000000000000000065] or                     000365
26   equivalent.                                                          000366
210102   2 NNN         00000001000psch                                    000367
25Commissioning and trial operation                                       000368
26   Commissioning and trial operation of all units (e.g.                 000369
26   treatment plant, pressure booster pumps), valves and                 000370
26   other functional units of this bill of quantities.                   000371
26                                                                        000372
26   After completion of the assembly (hydraulic/electrical)              000373
26   an inspection walk takes place.                                      000374
26   The end of assembly is to be notified in writing to                  000375
26   site management.                                                     000376
26   The establishing of the end of assembly relates only to              000377
26   the visual assessment. In doing so the completeness of               000378
26   the scope of supply and of the execution is checked.                 000379
26   After it has been successfully established that the                  000380
26   assembly is completed, the commissioning takes place,                000381
26   which is to be notified in writing to site management.               000382
26                                                                        000383
26   Commissioning and assembly are separated in time from                000384
26   one another. The commissioning can only take place                   000385
26   after completion of the electrical equipment. The                    000386
26   resulting costs for the renewed travel of the required               000387
26   personnel are to be included in the EP incl. all                     000388
26   ancillary costs, subsistence allowances, travel costs                000389
26   etc.                                                                 000390
26                                                                        000391
26   In doing so the following tests are carried out:                     000392
26   Pressure test of the overall plant. DIN EN 805 / DIN                 000393
26   4279, test pressure according to requirement PN 10 for               000394
26   all plant parts in the inlet of the clean water tanks /              000395
26   test pressure PN 16 for all plant parts from the clean               000396
26   water pumping station. The proof is to be documented in              000397
26   writing.                                                             000398
26   Checking of the equipment set-up, optimisation of the                000399
26   place of installation                                                000400
26   Test run until the intended operation of all plant                   000401
26   parts is proven.                                                     000402
26                                                                        000403
26   The commissioning takes place at the same time as the                000404
26   AN electrical engineering and is divided into:                       000405
26   Individual commissioning for all units / measurements                000406
26   incl. setting and adjustment of all required mechanical              000407
26   and electrical parameters.                                           000408
26   Commissioning of the entire plant in connection with                 000409
26   the interaction of all units / measurements / signal                 000410
26   transmitters etc., incl. setting and adjustment of all               000411
26   required mechanical and electrical parameters.                       000412
26   During the commissioning the PLC program is to be                    000413
26   optimised.                                                           000414
26                                                                        000415
26   For this, independent coordination of dates with the AN              000416
26   electrical engineering.                                              000417
26   After commissioning has taken place a trial operation                000418
26   is carried out.                                                      000419
26   With the trial operation an intensive support of the                 000420
26   operator's personnel (at least 1d/week) is to be                     000421
26   provided for the duration of 4 weeks.                                000422
26   To be included in the price are all required measuring               000423
26   instruments, personnel, aids and travel costs.                       000424
26                                                                        000425
26   It is pointed out that interruptions of the trial                    000426
26   operation for which the AN is responsible result in a                000427
26   corresponding extension of this trial operation. In the              000428
26   case of larger interruptions the trial operation is                  000429
26   broken off and is to be restarted from the beginning                 000430
26   after the problems have been remedied.                               000431
26   Basic settings changed in the running-in / optimisation              000432
26   operation are to be documented in a commissioning                    000433
26   report.                                                              000434
26                                                                        000435
26   The aim during this period is to optimise the                        000436
26   expenditure of personnel and energy. Furthermore the                 000437
26   automation is to be coordinated with the telecontrol                 000438
26   system (fault messages etc.).                                        000439
210102   3 NNN         00000001000psch                                    000440
25Analytical proof of guaranteed values                                   000441
26   The functional capability of the treatment plant is to               000442
26   be proven by sampling. For this the following analyses               000443
26   of an independent and certified laboratory are to be                 000444
26   submitted:                                                           000445
26                                                                        000446
26   In total 3 times at intervals of two weeks until the                 000447
26   end of the trial operation a small chemical-technical                000448
26   analysis with microbiology raw water and clean water                 000449
26   (after treatment)                                                    000450
26                                                                        000451
26   The following values are to be determined at least in                000452
26   each case:                                                           000453
26   Temperature and pH on site                                           000454
26   Calcite dissolution capacity                                         000455
26   Arsenic                                                              000456
26   Turbidity                                                            000457
26   CO2                                                                  000458
26   Oxygen                                                               000459
26   Odour                                                                000460
26   Freedom from germs ([PERSON_00000000000000000160]                    000461
26   bacteria, Escherichia coli, enterococci, culturable                  000462
26   microorganisms as colony count at 22 øC and 36 øC).                  000463
26                                                                        000464
