25Disinfection of arsenic removal filters                                 001855
26   After completion of the installation flushing, a                     001856
26   separate disinfection of the open arsenic removal                    001857
26   filters with hydrogen peroxide is to be carried out                  001858
26   according to manufacturer's recommendation GEH©.                     001859
26   The disinfectant, e.g. 1 container Veolia Hydrex 9561                001860
26   per filter, is to be introduced into the filter.                     001861
26   After an exposure time of at least 2 hours, a                        001862
26   disinfection flushing in upflow to remove the PER029                 001863
26   loaded with disinfectant from the adsorber bed,                      001864
26   backwash velocity 26 m/h, will to be carried out;                    001865
26   flushing until the outflow water is free of turbidity                001866
26   and for multiple water exchange in the filter bed,                   001867
26   duration at least 10 minutes.                                        001868
