26   Pipelines of stainless PER89                                         002009
26   General regulations for execution:                                   002010
26                                                                        002011
26   The requirements and designs listed below are to be                  002012
26   complied with and to be included in the price of the                 002013
26   respective pipeline items.                                           002014
26                                                                        002015
26   Connection points:                                                   002016
26   All connection points (position, dimension) are to be                002017
26   surveyed exactly on site. The details in the tender                  002018
26   documents do not release the bidder from this                        002019
26   obligation. Subsequent claims based on failure to carry              002020
26   out the survey are not recognised.                                   002021
26                                                                        002022
26   Venting/air admission and drains                                     002023
26   Unless otherwise required, venting/ air admission                    002024
26   facilities are to be provided at unavoidable high                    002025
26   points of liquid-carrying pipelines and drain                        002026
26   facilities at low points.                                            002027
26                                                                        002028
26   Pipe connections                                                     002029
26   All pipelines must be connected with easily detachable               002030
26   screw, clamp or compression connections or, for nominal              002031
26   diameters > DN 50, exclusively with flange connections               002032
26   to each other as well as to the tanks, wall                          002033
26   penetrations, valves, measuring devices etc. For                     002034
26   connections of different metallic materials (e.g.                    002035
26   filter tank - stainless steel line, but also components              002036
26   with non-conductive external corrosion protection, e.g.              002037
26   EKB) including supports, clamps etc., an electrical                  002038
26   separation "insulating flange" is to be provided to                  002039
26   prevent contact corrosion.                                           002040
26   Surcharges to the usual flange connections of the                    002041
26   nominal diameters to be offered in this LV for                       002042
26   producing an electrical separation point at flange                   002043
26   connection to avoid corrosion consisting of:                         002044
26   on piece insulating flange gasket,                                   002045
26   insulating sleeves, one piece per hole                               002046
26   insulating washers, two pieces per hole                              002047
26   steel washers, two pieces per hole                                   002048
26   are to be included in the unit prices of the valves to               002049
26   be installed.                                                        002050
26                                                                        002051
26   For electrical consumers installed in stainless steel                002052
26   pipelines (valves,measuring devices etc.), earthing                  002053
26   lugs for connection by others on site of an earthing                 002054
26   cable connection must in addition be welded onto the                 002055
26   adjoining stainless steel pipeline parts.                            002056
26                                                                        002057
26   Drinking-water-carrying pipelines from DN 65 and                     002058
26   larger, in flange-saving design, incl. all necessary                 002059
26   components (e.g. welding flanges etc.) welding                       002060
26   consumables and auxiliary materials, in particular                   002061
26   observing the following specification:                               002062
26   permissible component size max. fitting length 5.000 mm              002063
26   max. fitting width for outlets and bends 1.500 mm                    002064
26   Material: all pipes, bends, reducers and flanges in                  002065
26   material number 1.4571                                               002066
26   Pipes: longitudinally welded and pickled round pipes  v              002067
26   = 1,0, DIN EN 10216-5.                                               002068
26   The minimum wall thickness of the pipes is to be                     002069
26   designed according to the max. operating pressures                   002070
26   occurring acc. to AD-Merkblatt B0 and B1 and the                     002071
26   structural requirements, whereby the max. deflection of              002072
26   the pipeline in the ready-for-operation state is set at              002073
26   one four-hundredth of the span. A structural proof is                002074
26   to be provided on request of site management.                        002075
26   If the requirements from structural analysis or welded               002076
26   connections result in smaller wall thicknesses, at                   002077
26   least the following wall thicknesses are nevertheless                002078
26   to be complied with:                                                 002079
26   DN 10 - 32: 2,0 mm                                                   002080
26   DN 40 - 80: 2,0 mm                                                   002081
26   DN 100 - 150: 2,6 mm                                                 002082
26   DN 200: 2,9 mm                                                       002083
26   DN 250: 3,0 mm                                                       002084
26   DN 300 - 350: 3,2 mm                                                 002085
26   DN 400 - 500: 4,0 mm                                                 002086
26   DN 600 - 1000: 5,0 mm                                                002087
26                                                                        002088
26   Bends: longitudinally welded and pickled bends type 3;               002089
26   from DN 400 R = d + 100                                              002090
26   Reducers: longitudinally welded and pickled reducers;                002091
26   overall length according to DIN EN 10253; minimum wall               002092
26   thickness according to pipe wall thickness                           002093
26   Flanges: acc. to DIN EN 1092-1                                       002094
26                                                                        002095
26   Requirements for the manufacturing plant of the                      002096
26   pipelines:                                                           002097
26   All fittings are to be manufactured at the works ready               002098
26   for assembly in ferrite-free rooms. Manufacture in                   002099
26   rooms in which ferritic steels are also processed is                 002100
26   not permitted. In addition, only ferrite-free tools and              002101
26   lifting gear may be used for processing the fittings.                002102
26   The ferrite-free manufacture is agreed not as an                     002103
26   ancillary service but as a main service.                             002104
26   Site welds are permitted only in exceptional cases and               002105
26   only with express approval of site management. The                   002106
26   specialist pipeline company is to be named with the bid              002107
26   and a proof of its ferrite-free manufacture is to be                 002108
26   submitted.                                                           002109
26                                                                        002110
26   Fusion welding processes                                             002111
26   For welding processes for the aforementioned fittings,               002112
26   exclusively the individual processes acc. to ISO 4063                002113
26   13 gas-shielded metal arc welding 14 tungsten inert gas              002114
26   welding are permitted. The material with the number                  002115
26   1.4576 is to be used as welding filler material.                     002116
26                                                                        002117
26   Weld seam quality                                                    002118
26   The quality level for imperfections EN DIN 5817 group D              002119
26   applies as minimum requirements with the exception of                002120
26   reference no. 2017 (acc. to ISO 6520-1). For this                    002121
26   reference number EN DIN 5817 group B applies as minimum              002122
26   requirement.                                                         002123
26                                                                        002124
26   Quality assurance                                                    002125
26   For quality assurance of the weld seams, a                           002126
26   non-destructive test according to ISO 17637 is carried               002127
26   out. This test can be carried out by site management or              002128
26   by an independent expert commissioned separately by the              002129
26   building owner during and after fabrication of the                   002130
26   fittings. Should there be disagreement between the AN                002131
26   and site management or the expert about the quality                  002132
26   assessment, the AG can additionally order a                          002133
26   radiographic test.                                                   002134
26                                                                        002135
26   Post-treatment of the fittings                                       002136
26   All pipe fittings are to be pickled and passivated in a              002137
26   full bath after welding. For transport to the site, all              002138
26   openings of the fittings are to be closed with covers                002139
26   and packed in suitable fabric-reinforced film at least               002140
26   0,5 mm thick.                                                        002141
26                                                                        002142
26   Assembly of the fittings                                             002143
26   The fittings are to be delivered to the site free of                 002144
26   damage.                                                              002145
26   No ferritic tools may be used on site for moving and                 002146
26   assembling the fittings. Only stainless steels,                      002147
26   plastics or fabric slings are permitted. If ferritic                 002148
26   contamination is found after assembly, the pipes and                 002149
26   fittings concerned are to be removed and pickled and                 002150
26   passivated in a full bath at the works at the expense                002151
26   of the party responsible. To ensure nearly stress-free               002152
26   assembly, all pipe supports are to be made                           002153
26   height-adjustable.                                                   002154
26                                                                        002155
26   Before acceptance, in coordination with site                         002156
26   management, all films are to be removed, the pipelines               002157
26   given a final cleaning and oiled with an agent suitable              002158
26   for drinking water.                                                  002159
26   General notes on piping are also to be observed.                     002160
26                                                                        002161
26   Flanges:                                                             002162
26   The use of flanges PN 10 (according to EN                            002163
26   1092-1:2018-1) with reduced flange thickness is                      002164
26   generally permitted if, for the nominal diameters                    002165
26   tendered, the tightness of the pipe joint is proven by               002166
26   calculation according to the AD bulletin (calculation                002167
26   is to be enclosed with the bid)                                      002168
26                                                                        002169
26   Flange bolts / nuts:                                                 002170
26   Bolts and washers: min. 1.4401; nuts: min. 1.4571                    002171
26                                                                        002172
26   Reducers:                                                            002173
26   Eccentric or concentric design according to the                      002174
26   technical requirements in the pipe system, wall                      002175
26   thicknesses and other requirements as above.                         002176
26                                                                        002177
26   Saddle nozzles:                                                      002178
26   ###: made from pipe bend. Wall thicknesses and other                 002179
26   requirements as above.                                               002180
26                                                                        002181
26   Adjusting and dismantling pieces:                                    002182
26   All spindles and nuts of 1.4571. All sealing elements                002183
26   of KTW- and DVGW W270-approved material. Wall                        002184
26   thicknesses and other requirements as above.                         002185
26                                                                        002186
26   Pipe support and pipe holders:                                       002187
26   Height-adjustable sectional steel structures for                     002188
26   support, P074-, suspension and special fixings                       002189
26   including fixing material such as anchors or stainless               002190
26   steel screws. The supports / suspensions must be                     002191
26   designed so that all loads occurring in operation are                002192
26   safely absorbed.                                                     002193
26   The pipes are to be installed by means of 2-part flat                002194
26   steel pipe clamps with PVC insert.                                   002195
26   The supports are to be protected with suitable                       002196
26   protective film until acceptance of the plant.                       002197
26                                                                        002198
26   ALL VALVES AND OTHER MACHINES AND EQUIPMENT ARE TO BE                002199
26   ASSEMBLED STRESS-FREE, OBSERVING MANUFACTURER'S                      002200
26   INSTRUCTIONS (for example regarding calming sections)!               002201
26                                                                        002202
26                                                                        002203
26   Billing notes:                                                       002204
26                                                                        002205
26   Unless expressly stated otherwise in the item text, the              002206
26   SUPPLY AND READY-FOR-OPERATION ASSEMBLY IS TO BE                     002207
26   INCLUDED IN THE PRICE in the unit prices for the                     002208
26   pipeline, fitting and pipeline accessory items.                      002209
26   The billing length of the stainless steel pipelines is               002210
26   determined incl. the flanges and fittings, etc.,                     002211
26   machines (e.g. pumps, blowers), valves and filter                    002212
26   housings (air filtration) are however not measured                   002213
26   through. In this respect the flanges and fittings are                002214
26   to be priced as SURCHARGE TO THE RESPECTIVE PIPELINE                 002215
26   with corresponding nominal diameter.                                 002216
26   WELD SEAMS are not paid separately. They are TO BE                   002217
26   INCLUDED IN THE PRICE in the items of the fittings and               002218
26   flanges.                                                             002219
26   Flange connection sets (bolts, washers, gaskets and -                002220
26   where required - galvanic isolation) are TO BE INCLUDED              002221
26   IN THE PRICE in the items of the flanges or valves.                  002222
